# Rules for Cursor AI Agent

[Project Context]
Type = Next.js App Router (TypeScript)
Architecture = On-Premise (Standalone Server per Client)
Styling = CSS Modules (*.module.css) + Material UI Abstraction in /components/ui

[Styling Guidelines]
1. ALWAYS use CSS Modules for component-level styling (`NombreComponente.module.css` junto al componente).
2. NEVER import @mui/material components directly in pages/features. Import them from `@/components/ui` or `@/utils/MyButtons`.
3. Keep global reset, fonts, and CSS variables in `app/globals.css`.
4. Component design must be responsive, modern, and clean.
5. Pages in `app/` only compose; reusable UI lives in `src/components/`.

[Folder Structure]
1. `src/components/` — UI (ui, chat, layout, providers). Each component has its own `*.module.css`.
2. `src/utils/` — helpers (api, auth, constants, spCatalog) y `MyButtons` (wrapper MUI ISG).
3. Prefer `@/components/ui` for generic UI; use `@/utils/MyButtons` for brand primary/secondary buttons.
4. `src/lib/chat/` — chat orchestration (tool routing, windowing, truncation, local agent).
5. `src/types/` — shared TypeScript DTOs.

[Architecture & API]
1. This app is hosted ON-PREMISE on the client's own Windows Server/Domain.
2. Do NOT hardcode central Cloud/SaaS URLs. Use relative paths `/api/...` or `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`.
3. Authenticate using JWT stored securely (HTTP-only cookie or LocalStorage as fallback).

[Code Quality]
1. Strict TypeScript types for all DTOs and Props.
2. Clean code, well-commented functions, handle loading and error states explicitly.

[Multi-LLM]
1. Catálogo, BYOK y resolución de modelos viven en src/lib/llm/ (registry, resolveModel, byokStorage).
2. No hardcodear API keys; usar env, BYOK cifrado o helpers de resolveModel.
3. Nuevos modelos: actualizar MODEL_CATALOG, documentación en docs/LLM.md y selector vía /api/chat/providers.
4. Prioridad de claves: BYOK usuario > env empresa > env free tier.
5. Rutas API: /api/chat (modelId + fallback 429), /api/chat/providers, /api/settings/ia.